        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/warlock-header-closer.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>This probably feels like a bit of an odd place to start, but Warlock: Dungeons & Dragons isn't Fable. Yet, when I sat down to watch <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pNw0sh481bA\">developer Invoke Studios' Gamescom demo of Warlock</a> with no real idea of what to expect, it was the first thing that popped into my mind. Not because of its striking fantasy landscape - crooked hovels huddled awkwardly amid a vast sprawl of ragged coastline, jagged mountains, and, in the distance, an imposing tower looming over all - but rather the moment early on when Warlock's warrior protagonist Kaatri enters the town of Crickshank and is immediately welcomed with a couple of fruity insults from the locals.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/warlock-dungeons-dragons-gamescom-preview\">Read more</a></p>",
